-- an automorphism of an oriented molecule: a relabelling that preserves the graph and the handedness
-- at every atom. This is the group whose orbits are the equivalence classes a spectrum actually
-- reports: the field computes the orbits of the bond graph alone (the automorphism partition of the
-- nuclei, from which 13C signal counts and intensity ratios are read off), which gets homotopic
-- nuclei right and diastereotopic nuclei wrong, because diastereotopicity is not a property of the
-- graph.
OrAuto : Oriented → Type 0
OrAuto S = (a : Auto (or-mol S)) × ((x : mol-atoms (or-mol S)) → or-hand S (auto-fun (or-mol S) a x) ≡ or-hand S x)
